    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-01",
      "block_type": "definition",
      "heading": "Title, key, scale and orientation",
      "text": "A map represents selected features of an area using symbols and a stated spatial framework. Its title identifies the place or topic, its key explains symbols, its scale links map and ground distance, and its orientation shows direction. Read those elements together before interpreting a feature. A colour or line means what the supplied key states, rather than what a learner remembers from a different map.",
      "claim_ids": [
