    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The title helps establish purpose and extent. A population-density map and a topographical map of the same area select different information. A title can also include a date, while further source notes may specify the observation period. An old map remains useful for historical study but should not be treated as a complete current record without verification. The area shown also limits how widely an observation can be extended.",
      "claim_ids": [
