    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A key can distinguish roads, paths, rivers, buildings, land use and other features through colour, shape or line style. Similar-looking symbols can have different meanings, so identify the actual legend entry. A coloured area might mean woodland, cultivation, water or an administrative class depending on the map. A map answer should connect the feature to its keyed meaning rather than infer land use from colour alone.",
