    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Symbols are selective and often generalised. A point symbol can represent a building too small to draw at its true dimensions; a road line may be wider than its exact scaled ground width. This improves readability but limits measurement of the symbol itself. A school symbol locates a service building; it does not show the number of pupils, opening times or condition. Those require other data.",
