    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-06",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Scale can be shown in three ways. A representative fraction (RF), such as 1:50 000, is a ratio with no units. A linear scale, or scale bar, is a line divided into labelled ground distances. A statement scale, or word scale, gives the relationship in words, such as \"1 cm represents 0.5 km\". To convert 1:50 000, note that 1 cm represents 50 000 cm; divide by 100 to get 500 m, then by 1 000 to get 0.5 km. If a map is resized on a screen, only the scale bar stays correct, because it changes size with the map.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.2.01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.2.01-2",
