    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Large and small scale refer to the representative fraction, not the sheet's physical size. A larger-scale map shows a smaller area in greater potential detail than a smaller-scale one at comparable sheet dimensions. The maps in these notes use 1:50 000, a large scale that shows roads, buildings, rivers and contours clearly.",
