    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Orientation is read from a north arrow or the labelled coordinate framework. Do not assume the top of a rotated page is north. Directions from one feature to another require the correct starting point and orientation. A northward line and an eastward line make a right angle in the local compass framework used for the exercise. The map's stated north reference should be retained when measuring bearings.",
