    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Grid north, true north and magnetic north are distinct references. A map task can specify a bearing from its provided grid-north arrow. A compass in the field responds to magnetic direction, and corrections depend on place and date. Do not import a correction printed for another country. The teaching calculations use the supplied map reference and do not require an invented magnetic adjustment.",
