    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-10",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A consistent training plan can use metre coordinates for original features: A at (2,000,2,000), B (4,000,2,000), C (4,000,4,000) and D (2,000,4,000), with x east and y north. These positions form a two-kilometre square. A–B lies eastward, A–D northward and A–C north-eastward. The numbers define geometry for the exercise rather than survey coordinates of real named buildings.",
