      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The most useful reading sequence is to identify the title and extent, decode the relevant symbols, check scale and north, then locate the features needed. A calculation should retain its measurements and units; an interpretation should name its mapped evidence. These habits support distance, area, slope, bearings and land-use work without relying on unprovided knowledge about the place.\n\n![Training map: title, key, scale and grid north](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-4.2-002-INTERP-answer.png)",
      "claim_ids": [
