    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-16",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Scale checking can use a known interval. At 1:50,000, a one-kilometre grid interval spans two centimetres at intended print size. If an on-screen image shows it at another physical size, a ruler measurement from the screen needs adjustment through a valid bar or supplied geometry. The ground relation has not changed because the viewer zoomed. A task should preserve enough scale information for an honest measurement.",
      "claim_ids": [
