    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-17",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A scale bar should have labelled units and intervals appropriate to the exercise. A line marked zero,one,two kilometres supports reading half-kilometre lengths by proportion if the resolution allows. A short fuzzy image cannot justify unlimited decimal precision. Retain the method and state a reasonable estimate. The scale is a measurement aid rather than evidence that every symbol is drawn at its true width.",
