    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.2.01-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Orientation can be checked against two reference points. If the grid's x increases east and y increases north, a point with larger x but unchanged y lies east. A point with lower y lies south. Those relationships remain even if the page is turned, provided the reference direction is turned with it. Do not use the current screen's top as a replacement for the supplied north.",
